  "notes": "Integrated stereo amplifier, 45 W + 45 W into 8 ohms. Inputs and outputs follow the 'Ports' list of the info sheet: Phono (MM), CD, Tuner, Line, Recorder-1/-2 playback in, Recorder-1/-2 REC out, speaker A/B switches, headphone jack. NOT stated in the info sheet and assumed: RCA jacks for all line/phono inputs and REC outputs, screw terminals (+/-) for the speakers, 6.3 mm jack for headphones - please check on the device. Controls from the info sheet: input (function) switching, volume, Speaker A / B switches, muting (remote), Source Direct, Bass and Treble (+/-8 dB), Balance. Loudness is mentioned as a circuit, but not whether it is a knob or a button, so it is left out. Modelling assumptions: the selected input goes to the speakers, the headphones and both REC outputs; muting silences speakers and headphones; volume at MIN is treated as silent; Source Direct, Bass, Treble and Balance change the sound, not the signal path. Whether plugging in headphones switches off the speakers is not stated and is not modelled. Start positions (CD, Speakers A on, volume low) are app defaults. Left out: the switched AC outlet (socket type not stated), the phono ground terminal and the remote control. The archived product page also shows 'Bluetooth / Digital inputs', but that belongs to the successor PMA-600NE shown there.",
